From: Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>
Subject: mips: early_printk_8250: poll THRE only, not TEMT

prom_putchar() polls both THRE (bit 5, TX holding register empty) and
TEMT (bit 6, TX shift register empty). On the Airoha EN7523 UART used
in EcoNet EN751627 SoCs, TEMT is not reliably asserted between chars.

With a finite timeout, prom_putchar() times out on TEMT and silently
drops the character. Change to poll THRE only: THRE means the TX
holding register is ready to accept the next byte, which is the correct
condition for all MIPS 8250 UARTs.

Also set the earlycon timeout to 10000 for EN751627 (in init.c prom_init)
so prom_putchar does not skip the write. This is safe with THRE-only
polling since TEMT is no longer the bottleneck.

Signed-off-by: Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>
---
--- a/arch/mips/econet/init.c
+++ b/arch/mips/econet/init.c
@@ -36,6 +36,15 @@
 /* 1. Bring up early printk. */
 void __init prom_init(void)
 {
+#if defined(CONFIG_SOC_ECONET_EN751627)
+	/*
+	 * EN751627 (Airoha-family UART): use timeout=10000 so prom_putchar
+	 * does not skip the write. The THRE-only fix in early_printk_8250.c
+	 * ensures this timeout does not drop characters.
+	 */
+	setup_8250_early_printk_port(UART_BASE, UART_REG_SHIFT, 10000);
+#else
 	setup_8250_early_printk_port(UART_BASE, UART_REG_SHIFT, 0);
+#endif
 	_machine_restart = hw_reset;
 }
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/early_printk_8250.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/early_printk_8250.c
@@ -40,7 +40,12 @@
 		return;
 
 	timeout = serial8250_tx_timeout;
-	bits = UART_LSR_TEMT | UART_LSR_THRE;
+	/*
+	 * Poll THRE (TX holding register empty) only. TEMT (shift register
+	 * empty, bit 6) is not reliable on all platforms (e.g. Airoha EN7523)
+	 * and polling it causes prom_putchar to drop characters on timeout.
+	 */
+	bits = UART_LSR_THRE;
 
 	do {
 		status = serial_in(UART_LSR);
